{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short && git branch --show-current && git log --oneline --decorate -12 && git diff --stat origin/main...HEAD && git diff --find-renames --check origin/main...HEAD && gh pr view 14 --repo mrkkucharski/vgt --json number,title,state,isDraft,baseRefName,headRefName,mergeable,reviewDecision,body,commits,files,comments'","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"body\":\"Closes #9\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nSee issue #9 for details.\",\"comments\":[],\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-07-18T18:16:27Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"marekkucharski@mini.local\",\"id\":\"\",\"login\":\"\",\"name\":\"Marek Kucharski\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Sonnet 5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-07-18T18:16:27Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Implements the key and chords analysis stages on top of #7's stage-cache\\nframework, per #9:\\n\\n- key.py: root/scale/confidence via Essentia's KeyExtractor when installed\\n  (optional, per docs/GOAL.md's Apple-Silicon-wheel caveat), falling back to\\n  librosa chroma correlated against the 24 Krumhansl-Schmuckler major/minor\\n  templates.\\n- chords.py: beat-aligned maj/min chord segments via madmom's CNN chord\\n  recognizer when installed, falling back to per-beat harmonic-chroma\\n  classified against 24 maj/min triad templates. Sub 2's shared beat grid\\n  (#8) isn't accepted on main yet, so the fallback detects its own\\n  lightweight beat grid via librosa purely to snap chord boundaries -- flagged\\n  in the module docstring to switch over once #8 lands. Every result is\\n  flagged `\\\"vocabulary\\\": \\\"maj_min\\\"` per the issue's vocabulary-limitation\\n  note. Raw per-beat classification was noisy (chatter between a root's\\n  major/minor reading), so a majority-vote smoothing pass over neighboring\\n  beats stabilizes it into musically plausible runs before segments are\\n  merged.\\n- Renders a plain-text chord-sheet artifact next to the sidecar\\n  (`<project>.vgt-chords.txt`) for by-eye verification.\\n- Harmonizes the internal detector signature to `(project_path, source,\\n  settings)` across all four stages (tempo/sections stay stubs) so an\\n  artifact-writing detector doesn't need a special case.\\n\\nVerified against the real fixture: detects Bb minor (confidence 0.91) and an\\n81-segment chord sequence with coherent i-VI-v-style runs.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"feat: detect key and beat-aligned maj/min chords from the reference mix\",\"oid\":\"4cf61d0ccd025a9711306d65090eb5ca12b3e6fa\"},{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-07-18T18:18:08Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"marekkucharski@mini.local\",\"id\":\"\",\"login\":\"\",\"name\":\"Marek Kucharski\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Sonnet 5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-07-18T18:18:08Z\",\"messageBody\":\"Adds README coverage for the key/chords detectors and the chord-sheet\\nartifact, and a dedicated test asserting hand-corrected key/chords values\\n(human_verified: true) survive a re-run -- the acceptance criteria call this\\nout explicitly for these two stages, beyond the existing tempo-only test.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs+test: document key/chords detectors, cover correction persistence\",\"oid\":\"95f9308afb45eb41b935ad2cb4c098cadf4c00a8\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"README.md\",\"additions\":11,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"pyproject.toml\",\"additions\":4,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/analysis.py\",\"additions\":30,\"deletions\":14,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/chords.py\",\"additions\":189,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"src/vgt/key.py\",\"additions\":88,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"ADDED\"},{\"path\":\"tests/test_analysis.py\",\"additions\":56,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"uv.lock\",\"additions\":754,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"headRefName\":\"issue-9-phase-1-key-beat-aligned-chords\",\"isDraft\":false,\"mergeable\":\"CONFLICTING\",\"number\":14,\"reviewDecision\":\"\",\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"Phase 1: key + beat-aligned chords\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
